## Decisions the spec didn't spell out

- **Expiry boundary**: an entry is expired at `setTime + ttlMs` (i.e. `now() >= expiresAt`), not just after it — "each expiring ttlMs after it was set".
- **`get` refreshes LRU recency but not the TTL**, since expiry is anchored to "when it was set".
- **`set` of an existing key counts as a use** for LRU (a refresh moves it to most-recent).
- **Expired entries are evicted before live ones** when a new key arrives at capacity, since expired ones count as absent.
- **`delete` of an expired key** returns `false` (it counts as absent) while still freeing its slot.
- No iteration API exists, so recency/expiry state is maintained lazily per operation; physical storage never exceeds `capacity`.

There are no other project checks (no lint/typecheck script; `bun test` is the only script).

